# Flink MCP Enterprise Server

Production-grade **Model Context Protocol (MCP)** server for [Apache Flink](https://flink.apache.org/).
Governed tool access to the Flink REST API and SQL Gateway ΓÇö secure by default, observable, and review-ready.

**Artifact:** `io.github.vaquarkhan:flink-mcp-server:0.2.0`  
**Repo:** https://github.com/vaquarkhan/flink-mcp-enterprise-server  
**License:** Apache-2.0

Compared to community Flink MCP projects ([Ashfaqbs/apache-flink-mcp-server](https://github.com/Ashfaqbs/apache-flink-mcp-server), [Cledar/flink-mcp](https://github.com/Cledar/flink-mcp)), this server adds a full **governance plane**: approval tokens, policy deny-lists, rate limits, circuit breakers, output DLP, hash-chained audit, Prometheus metrics, and fail-closed HTTP auth.

---

## Quick start

```bash
mvn clean package
# Tests run: 39+, Failures: 0

# stdio (read-only default) ΓÇö stdout = MCP JSON-RPC, stderr = logs
FLINK_REST_URL=http://localhost:8081 \
java -jar target/flink-mcp-server-0.2.0-all.jar

# HTTP (Bearer required)
MCP_FLINK_TRANSPORT=http \
MCP_FLINK_HTTP_BEARER_TOKEN=change-me \
FLINK_REST_URL=http://localhost:8081 \
java -jar target/flink-mcp-server-0.2.0-all.jar
```

Ops endpoints (HTTP mode): `GET /healthz`, `GET /readyz`, `GET /metrics` (Prometheus). MCP: `/mcp`.

---

## Default tool surface (read profile)

| Tool | Backend |
|------|---------|
| `get_cluster_info` | `GET /overview` |
| `get_flink_config` | `GET /config` |
| `list_taskmanagers` | `GET /taskmanagers` |
| `list_jobs` | `GET /jobs/overview` |
| `get_job` / `get_job_status` / `get_job_config` | job detail endpoints |
| `get_job_exceptions` / `get_job_metrics` / `list_checkpoints` | job diagnostics |
| `list_jars` | `GET /jars` |
| `run_sql_readonly` | SQL Gateway (SELECT/WITH/SHOW/DESCRIBE/EXPLAIN only) |

### Write tools (off until unlocked)

Require `MCP_FLINK_WRITE_ENABLED=true` **and** `MCP_FLINK_APPROVAL_SECRET`, plus a single-use HMAC approval token:

`trigger_savepoint`, `rescale_job`, `upload_jar`, `run_jar`, `stop_job`, `cancel_job`, `run_sql_ddl_dml`

```bash
java -cp target/flink-mcp-server-0.2.0-all.jar \
  io.github.vaquarkhan.flinkmcp.security.ApprovalTokens <secret> stop_job <jobId> 300
```

`upload_jar` also requires `MCP_FLINK_JAR_UPLOAD_ALLOW_DIRS` (fail-closed path allow-list).

### Resources

`flink://cluster/overview`, `flink://jobs`, `flink://health` (self + Flink + gateway ping),  
`flink://audit/recent`, `flink://metrics`, `flink://metrics/prometheus`

---

## Twelve-factor / cloud-native checklist

| Factor | Implementation |
|--------|----------------|
| I. Codebase | Single Maven module, Apache-2.0 |
| II. Dependencies | Explicit Maven coords (MCP SDK 1.1.3, Jetty 12, SLF4J/Logback) |
| III. Config | All settings via env (`Config.fromEnv()` + fail-fast `validate()`) |
| IV. Backing services | Flink REST + SQL Gateway treated as attached resources |
| V. Build/release/run | `mvn package` ΓåÆ thin + shaded `-all` jar |
| VI. Processes | Stateless MCP process; in-memory audit/metrics (export via resources/HTTP) |
| VII. Port binding | Self-contained Jetty (`MCP_FLINK_HTTP_HOST`/`PORT`) |
| VIII. Concurrency | Bounded backend pool (4ΓÇô32, queue 128, AbortPolicy) |
| IX. Disposability | Shutdown hook drains pool + stops Jetty |
| X. Dev/prod parity | Same jar; env switches transport/auth/writes |
| XI. Logs | **stderr only** (stdout reserved for MCP); MDC `trace=` on every line |
| XII. Admin processes | ApprovalTokens CLI; `/healthz` `/readyz` `/metrics` |

Extra production factors: **secure-by-default**, **DLP redaction**, **path-injection defense**, **circuit breaker**, **rate limit**, **policy engine**.

---

## Environment reference

| Variable | Default | Notes |
|----------|---------|-------|
| `FLINK_REST_URL` | `http://localhost:8081` | JobManager REST |
| `MCP_FLINK_GATEWAY_URL` | `http://localhost:8083` | SQL Gateway |
| `MCP_FLINK_REST_AUTH_HEADER` | ΓÇö | Optional `Bearer ΓÇª` / `Basic ΓÇª` to Flink |
| `MCP_FLINK_GATEWAY_AUTH_HEADER` | ΓÇö | Optional auth to Gateway |
| `MCP_FLINK_WRITE_ENABLED` | `false` | Master write switch |
| `MCP_FLINK_APPROVAL_SECRET` | ΓÇö | Required if writes enabled |
| `MCP_FLINK_APPROVAL_TTL_MS` | `300000` | Token TTL |
| `MCP_FLINK_READONLY_CALLER` | `false` | Force read-only caller |
| `MCP_FLINK_RPS` | `5` | Global rate limit |
| `MCP_FLINK_BREAKER_FAILURES` | `5` | Circuit breaker threshold |
| `MCP_FLINK_BREAKER_RESET_MS` | `30000` | Open ΓåÆ half-open window |
| `MCP_FLINK_MAX_BYTES` | `65536` | Output bound |
| `MCP_FLINK_DLP_ENABLED` | `true` | Redact secrets/JWT/email |
| `MCP_FLINK_TRANSPORT` | `stdio` | `stdio` \| `http` |
| `MCP_FLINK_HTTP_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Bind address |
| `MCP_FLINK_HTTP_PORT` | `8090` | HTTP port |
| `MCP_FLINK_HTTP_BEARER_TOKEN` | ΓÇö | **Required** for HTTP |
| `MCP_FLINK_TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS` | `30000` | Backend timeout |
| `MCP_FLINK_POLICY_FILE` | ΓÇö | Deny rules file |
| `MCP_FLINK_TOOLS_ALLOWED` | default reads | CSV allow-list |
| `MCP_FLINK_SCOPE_JOBS_ALLOW` | `*` | Job scope |
| `MCP_FLINK_SCOPE_JARS_ALLOW` | `*` | Jar scope |
| `MCP_FLINK_JAR_UPLOAD_ALLOW_DIRS` | ΓÇö | Required for `upload_jar` |
| `MCP_FLINK_MAX_SQL_CHARS` | `32768` | SQL size cap |
| `MCP_FLINK_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS` | `15000` | Drain timeout |
| `MCP_FLINK_LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | `DEBUG`/`INFO`/`WARN`/`ERROR` |

Policy file sample: [`config/policy.sample`](config/policy.sample)

---

## Security model

1. **Read-only by default** ΓÇö mutate/destructive tools not registered until writes unlocked.  
2. **Approval tokens** ΓÇö HMAC-SHA256, expiry, nonce anti-replay, job/jar scope binding.  
3. **Policy engine** ΓÇö `deny tool <glob>` / `deny job <glob>`; missing file = fail-closed.  
4. **HTTP** ΓÇö Bearer constant-time compare; refuses to start without token.  
5. **Input hygiene** ΓÇö ID charset + `..` reject; jar path allow-list; SQL length + readonly guard.  
6. **Output DLP** ΓÇö redacts keys, JWTs, PEM headers, emails, Bearer tokens; truncates.  
7. **Logs never on stdout** ΓÇö prevents MCP protocol corruption.

---

## Observability

- **Logs:** stderr Logback with `trace=<id>` MDC on every governance call.  
- **Metrics:** in-process counters + latency p50/p95/p99 ΓåÆ JSON resource + Prometheus (`/metrics` or `flink://metrics/prometheus`).  
- **Audit:** hash-chained ring (500) ΓåÆ `flink://audit/recent` + `verifyChain()`.  
- **Health:** `flink://health` and HTTP `/healthz`/`/readyz` (ready probes Flink REST).

